<title>GERMANY: Deutsche 96 net income up 4.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Deutsche 96 net income up 4.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net income			    2,200  vs 2,100</p>
<p>Group oper profit after risk</p>
<p>    provisions				    5,800  up 37 pct</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total	     886,000 vs 722,000</p>
<p>    Group lending volume		    410,000 up 31,000</p>
<p>    Customer deposits			 375,000 up 25 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Deutsche Bank AG. Results are in accordance with International Accounting Standards (IAS). Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast a net profit of 2.17 billion marks on average, with forecasts ranging from 2.14 to 2.20 billion marks.</p>
<p>Deutsche said the 23 percent growth in its balance sheet total was explained by an increase in trading activities as part of its investment banking business.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
